{
  "_comment": "Per-faction unit and ship names, the stat trade a distinctive name carries, the ONE unique unit every realm fields, and the two small bonuses. Owner-specified across 0.20.0–0.20.2.",
  "_naming": "English or the accepted English form, always — Longbowman, Janissary, Gendarme, Cataphract, Bardiche Axeman, Mountain Spearman. A native word is kept only where it is the name English actually uses for the thing (Azab, Jinete, Akinci, Coustillier, Stradiot, Druzhina). Names are shared across realms wherever sharing is honest, so no category has thirteen different words for the same job — but no realm is all-generic either, which was the fault of 0.20.1.",
  "_unique": "Exactly one land unit per realm carries \"unique\": true. It is that realm's signature — the thing a player picks the faction to field — and it carries the largest trade in the roster. Never a ship: the owner asked for a unique LAND unit.",
  "_skirmishers": "The skirmisher line is range 30, accuracy 0.3 — a javelin, sling or dart thrower. Javelineer, Slinger, Peltast, Kern, Bedouin Skirmisher. Handgunners and naphtha throwers were 0.20.1 mistakes and are gone: neither is a skirmishing weapon.",
  "_trades": "Only a distinctive name carries a stat trade; a shared plain name fields the base figures. Deltas are added to the base in data/units.json. Only hp, damage and strategicSpeed may vary — cost, size, upkeep and build time are identical in every realm.",

